Source: hamnews
Section: news
Priority: optional
Maintainer: KN6FLN <lweith@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: hamnews
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd
Suggests: hnlink, tin
Description: minimal INN news server for ham-radio usenet
 A stripped INN 2.7 in its own namespace (/etc/hamnews, /usr/lib/hamnews,
 /var/lib/hamnews, /var/spool/hamnews) so it coexists with inn2. It holds the
 ham.* groups that hnlink exchanges over a local radio net, and that FLAMP
 batches carry between nets. Read and post with any newsreader at
 localhost:119.

Package: hnlink
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, systemd
Recommends: direwolf
Suggests: hamnews
Description: broadcast usenet exchange over a local amateur radio net
 hnlink keeps the news servers on a radio net in sync. Stations announce what
 they hold; missing articles go out once as Reed-Solomon coded AX.25 UI frames
 through direwolf (KISS TCP) and every station that hears them decodes them,
 relaying across simplex hops. Includes a local status and posting page, and
 'hnlink batch'/'hnlink load' for moving rnews batches over FLAMP.

Package: itsjustnews
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: direwolf
Description: receive-only monitor that decodes hnlink traffic to plain text
 For anyone checking that hnlink stations send plain usenet and nothing that
 obscures meaning (47 CFR 97.113(a)(4)). It listens to direwolf's KISS port
 or a KISS capture file, explains every hnlink frame, reassembles the
 Reed-Solomon coded objects and prints every article in full. It has no
 transmit path.

Package: airtime
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, systemd
Recommends: direwolf
Description: channel use by callsign-SSID, from direwolf
 A receive-only AGW client of direwolf. It counts frames, bytes and estimated
 airtime per radio channel, callsign-SSID and direction (including this
 station's own transmissions, which KISS clients never see), with frame types,
 PIDs and channel occupancy. It serves a page, JSON and Prometheus metrics,
 and can write a pcap packet trace for Wireshark.
